name: evolved_qec_3edd1ff39077
description: Public-score best MAS from RSI-Exam qec_decoder_arena; use for this task
  only
backend: smolagents
agents:
  worker1:
    id: worker1
    role: worker
    agent_type: CodeAgent
    model_id: openai:deepseek-v4-flash-s2
    prompt: 'Generate a complete Python function for correlation-aware decoding of
      color-code quantum error correction data. Use the dev.npz data (dev_dets, dev_obs)
      to calibrate a decoder that accounts for correlated errors in the DEM hyperedges.
      The function must: (1) Parse the DEM text from setting["dem"]; (2) Build a weighted
      matching graph where edge weights are calibrated using dev data statistics;
      (3) Use PyMatching to decode with these calibrated weights; (4) Return a boolean
      array of shape [n_shots, n_observables]. Test your logic conceptually but output
      the COMPLETE function code. Use only stim, pymatching, numpy, scipy. Output
      ONLY Python code, no explanations.'
    tools:
    - subset_read_context
    - subset_read_public
    - subset_read_history
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.3
    device: null
  worker2:
    id: worker2
    role: worker
    agent_type: CodeAgent
    model_id: openai:deepseek-v4-flash-s2
    prompt: 'Generate a complete Python function for a reweighted MWPM decoder for
      color codes that uses dev data for calibration. The published DEM is miscalibrated.
      Your function must: (1) Read the DEM from setting["dem"]; (2) Analyze dev_dets
      and dev_obs from setting to compute empirical error rates per detector; (3)
      Re-weight the DEM hyperedges using these empirical rates; (4) Run PyMatching
      on the reweighted DEM; (5) Return boolean predictions [n_shots, n_observables].
      Include explicit dtype conversion to bool. Output ONLY the complete Python function
      code. Use only stim, pymatching, numpy, scipy.'
    tools:
    - subset_read_context
    - subset_read_public
    - subset_read_history
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.25
    device: null
  worker3:
    id: worker3
    role: worker
    agent_type: CodeAgent
    model_id: openai:GLM-5.3-Flash
    prompt: 'Generate a robust fallback decoder function for color codes that handles
      edge cases and ensures correct output format. The function must: (1) Accept
      setting dict and dets array; (2) If primary decoding fails, use a simple independent-observable
      model (most probable observable per shot based on dev_obs statistics); (3) Ensure
      output is boolean dtype with shape [n_shots, n_observables]; (4) Include timing
      checks to stay under setting["meta"]["decode_budget_sec"]; (5) Validate that
      no NaN or inf values appear. Output ONLY the complete Python function code.
      Use only stim, pymatching, numpy, scipy.'
    tools:
    - subset_read_context
    - subset_read_public
    - subset_read_history
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    device: null
  aggregator:
    id: aggregator
    role: aggregator
    agent_type: CodeAgent
    model_id: openai:GLM-5.3-W4A8
    prompt: 'Merge the decoder components from workers into a complete, working /app/methods/main/solver.py
      file. The final decode(setting, dets) function must: (1) Try the best correlation-aware
      decoder first; (2) Fall back to reweighted MWPM if that fails or times out;
      (3) Use robust fallback as last resort; (4) ALWAYS return boolean array of shape
      [n_shots, n_observables]; (5) Include timing to respect decode_budget_sec; (6)
      Handle all four settings (d5, d5_Z, d7, d9) correctly. Write the COMPLETE solver.py
      file. Verify: boolean dtype, correct shape, no imports beyond stim/pymatching/numpy/scipy.
      Use subset_write_candidate to write the final file, then subset_preflight to
      check it.'
    tools:
    - subset_read_context
    - subset_read_public
    - subset_read_history
    - subset_write_candidate
    - subset_preflight
    - subset_public_python
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.15
    device: null
topology:
  reports_to:
    worker1:
    - aggregator
    worker2:
    - aggregator
    worker3:
    - aggregator
execution:
  parallel_workers: true
  timeout: 600
  max_retries: 0
successful_tasks:
- q: RSI-Exam qec_decoder_arena
  notes: Best configuration on public cases; do not compare raw metrics across tasks
